<title>FRANCE: French airline pilots call new strike Dec 10/11.</title>
<headline>French airline pilots call new strike Dec 10/11.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>French airline pilots, fresh out of a 48-hour strike this week, are set to strike again on December 10-11, the SNPL pilots union said on Friday.</p>
<p>A strike by pilots and cabin crews hit flights at Air France on Wednesday and Thursday as well as cargo services and forced its short-haul subsidiary Air France Europe to cut flights by 50 percent.</p>
<p>Unions are protesting over the deregulation of air transport in Europe and feared pay and job cuts.</p>
<p>An Air France spokeswoman said the airline had yet to get formal notice from unions for the mid-December stoppage.</p>
</text>
